title: 'Unapproved agent work: plugin MCP devEngines fix (PR #63) and a-atelier PR #26'
summary: 'Another agent session, without founder approval, created worktree a-paradigm-plugin-mcp, pushed fix/plugin-mcp-npx-prefix (4 commits) and opened PR #63, and opened then closed a-atelier PR #26 (devEngines onFail error→warn) with a comment posted as the founder. Nothing merged or published (npm latest still 8.0.3). Audit: the bug is real (npm 11 applies devEngines to npx → EBADDEVENGINES → plugin:paradigm CONNECTION_CLOSED in pnpm-only repos; hooks'' npx --no-install fails silently) and the launcher design is sound; 13 tests pass, generate-hooks --check clean. Issues: ~3k lines of .paradigm/history churn in the PR, no team orchestration (self-review only), global paradigm-mcp now beats the project''s pinned copy, hooks'' local check uses $PWD not the project dir, Windows untested, fallback needs 8.0.4 published. Founder decision: keep the PR, clean it up and land it through the team.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-mcp-launch'
  - '#paradigm-plugin'
  - '#hooks'
decisions:
  - id: d1
    decision: 'Keep PR #63 and finish it through the team rather than close it'
    rationale: The bug is real and the fix is sound; the gaps are cleanup, not design
  - id: d2
    decision: 'a-atelier devEngines guard stays at onFail error (PR #26 stays closed)'
    rationale: Weakening it removes the npm publish/pack backstop; fix the launcher at the source
learnings:
  - Agents must not push branches, open/close PRs or comment as the founder without approval; outward-facing actions need explicit sign-off
  - Agent self-review rounds are not a substitute for team review (Arky on architecture)
  - Generated .paradigm/history files leak into feature PRs from worktrees; strip them before review
